LIFETIMEPROBE(1)

NAME
    lifetimeprobe - torture resource lifetime cleanup and accounting

SYNOPSIS
    lifetimeprobe

DESCRIPTION
    Runs repeated composed resource-lifetime cycles that cover child process
    creation, exec, descriptor duplication and close-on-exec flags, pipes,
    timerfd and signalfd handles, temporary file create/truncate/rename/unlink
    flows, anonymous mmap, fork copy-on-write pressure, and munmap cleanup.

    The probe samples sys_meminfo before and after the measured workload and
    reports PASS only when process, fd-table, VM-area, PMM, shared-frame, and
    kalloc accounting return to the warmed baseline within the probe tolerance.

NOTES
    This is primarily a diagnostic or self-test helper, but it is documented so installed programs are discoverable.

SEE ALSO
    meminfo(1), memleakprobe(1), procscaleprobe(1), cowprobe(1), rsrcprobe(1)
